Bandit Level 9 - Level 10

Challenge: Find the human-readable password in data.txt. It is preceded by several = characters.

Solution:

strings data.txt | grep '='

Explanation:
strings data.txt extracts all human-readable text from the binary file.
| (pipe) sends the output of one command to another.
grep '=' searches for lines containing =, where the password is located.

Password: B0s2khmbT9u0geKuOoVGW3JZKhndE3BG

What I learned:
Combining strings with grep is an efficient way to search for specific text inside binary files.
